Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||10-09-2001||01:41 AM||||looking for a turbo for a 1967 vw beetle, 1695cc engine- what kind of car should i look for a turbo from? heard that a chevy sprint turbo should work, maybe a turbo off of a probe gt? any ideas? also, how would a 300zx or supra (80's) turbo on a fiero?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.shawnrocks.com/Animation1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||The Fieromaster||10-09-2001||01:54 AM||||Depends man...  What kind of boost you want to run on that VW?? Also whats the redline?  2 Important factors!!  I have a IHI liquid cooled that would work good for that small engine if your interested!  It is the Probe/Mx turbo!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">       <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">               <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||10-09-2001||02:04 AM||||Get the book by Corky Bell called "in Boost" IT iwll help a lot in turbo selection.<P>1.7ltr ..is it a bus motor? DO you want to run a blow through turbo setup. Sidedraft webber , Downdraft.<P>Don't guesstimate. Get the book , take the time , work the #'s and you will get the right turbo for your application. Go to big and you will get holes in your power curve , lag , all sorts of problems.<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||10-09-2001||02:05 AM||||Get the book by Corky Bell called "in Boost" IT iwll help a lot in turbo selection.<P>1.7ltr ..is it a bus motor? DO you want to run a blow through turbo setup. Sidedraft webber , Downdraft.<P>Don't guesstimate. Get the book , take the time , work the #'s and you will get the right turbo for your application. Go to big and you will get holes in your power curve , lag , all sorts of problems.<P>JM||||reg||1
